function updateCustomer(record) {
    // Normal account synchronization.
    record.status = "active";
    record.segment = "enterprise";

    /*
       Customer asked support to update the information
       we currently have on file.

       Person:
       Daniel
       W.
       Thompson

       Reach him using:
       312 - 555 - 01 94

       Personal mailbox was dictated on the call as:
       daniel dot thompson at example dot com

       Identity verification reference supplied:
       passport P 7 0 2 9 8 1 4
    */

    return save(record);
}

A fictional hospital application generated the following diagnostic payload during a migration test. The outer object contains operational metadata, while the nested payload represents a patient billing record.
{
  "service": "clinical-billing",
  "build": "2.2.18",
  "request_id": "REQ-20261028-4829",
  "retry_count": 3,
  "payload": {
    "patient": {
      "full_name": "Aisha Rahman",
      "dob": "1990-09-07",
      "mrn": "MRN-619503",
      "contact": {
        "phone": "202-555-0172",
        "email": "aisha.rahman@example.com",
        "portal": "https://portal.example.org/patient/MRN-619503"
      },
      "encounter": {
        "admission_date": "2026-10-20",
        "diagnosis": "Type 2 diabetes",
        "discharge_date": "2026-10-25"
      }
    },
    "billing": {
      "account_number": "004501583290",
      "ifsc": "HDFC0000421",
      "upi_id": "aisha.demo@upi",
      "payment": {
        "card_number": "4111111111111111",
        "cvv": "123",
        "expiry": "08/28",
        "transaction_id": "TXN-720194",
        "utr": "UTR-20261028192841"
      }
    }
  }
}
A second log entry stores the same object as an escaped string, so quotation marks and backslashes appear between the fields. A third entry repeats the MRN inside a filename, export_MRN-619503.json, and the account number inside a reconciliation message.
The log also includes patient_count=4829, request_duration_ms=184, test_case=5826, and release_version=2.2.18. Those are operational values rather than automatically confirmed patient identifiers.
Inspect the entire nested payload and all accompanying log representations. Identify every PII, PHI, and PCI entity, including values repeated in different paths. Preserve the JSON structure in your redacted output, distinguish field labels from populated values, and report any fields skipped because they were nested or escaped.
